WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:05.015
You learned the interactive
revocation list limits for GCC:

3
00:00:05.015 --> 00:00:08.162
twenty megabytes, and
ten seconds to download.

4
00:00:08.162 --> 00:00:09.719
You measured three lists,

5
00:00:09.719 --> 00:00:13.649
and the missing one became a
recorded finding instead of a crash.

6
00:00:13.649 --> 00:00:16.611
You checked a fictional tenant for GCC,

7
00:00:16.611 --> 00:00:20.312
and saw how the GCC limit
sets the C B five warning.

8
00:00:20.312 --> 00:00:23.407
Keep the measurement and
the check running every day,

9
00:00:23.407 --> 00:00:26.924
because a list that fits today
can cross the limit next month.

10
00:00:26.924 --> 00:00:30.271
Next is Module 6, time
separations from the logs:

11
00:00:30.271 --> 00:00:35.075
separation-to-block and
separation-to-revocation for every leaver.

12
00:00:35.075 --> 00:00:38.112
It builds on this module,
because a card's revocation

13
00:00:38.112 --> 00:00:40.780
reaches sign-in through
the revocation list.
